            {
                "entry_id": "897c70fd-39b7-39e6-841e-70b0422a6ad3",
                "word": "metaphysic",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "33841ab4-4b03-4acb-becb-88910e1d2b60",
                        "entry_id": "897c70fd-39b7-39e6-841e-70b0422a6ad3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "metaphysics"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2e67d902-8ea3-37a4-b4f5-30a822e3cab3",
                        "entry_id": "897c70fd-39b7-39e6-841e-70b0422a6ad3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The field of study of metaphysics."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4e79224-1f18-44f5-a4a6-07ff8891e01a",
                                "sense_id": "2e67d902-8ea3-37a4-b4f5-30a822e3cab3",
                                "text": "With reference to general Philosophy or Metaphysic proper, psychology may be viewed as a kind of common ground whereon thinkers of widely different schools may meet."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1b861cc6-e01a-36a1-b41f-30a0a435124d",
                        "entry_id": "897c70fd-39b7-39e6-841e-70b0422a6ad3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The metaphysical system of a particular philosopher or of a particular school of thought."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b74b7ce7-f01f-427b-8b3d-f9955b322ad2",
                                "sense_id": "1b861cc6-e01a-36a1-b41f-30a0a435124d",
                                "text": "A Neoplatonic metaphysic is the flip side of mysticism."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "347f1c31-6e7e-4f60-a3d2-705b48455a04",
                                "sense_id": "1b861cc6-e01a-36a1-b41f-30a0a435124d",
                                "text": "The uncertain conclusions of an ill-conducted analogy, and a false metaphysic, were mixed with a few simple precepts derived from observation, which probably made the whole of the science of prognostication in its earliest and purest state."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6aab30c9-0367-44e3-8f20-f9b58ea88b3a",
                                "sense_id": "1b861cc6-e01a-36a1-b41f-30a0a435124d",
                                "text": "It should be pointed out to the prospective reader that he will not find here the systematic presentation of a metaphysic."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ce80dbea-e649-3b71-b8f3-33de5d2bf0f8",
                        "entry_id": "897c70fd-39b7-39e6-841e-70b0422a6ad3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fundamental principle or key concept."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "53acebb7-3571-42db-9199-9fb413a0d733",
                                "sense_id": "ce80dbea-e649-3b71-b8f3-33de5d2bf0f8",
                                "text": "What we need as a metaphysic and what the logical realists are at least glimpsing, is the principle of contradiction."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
